{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees\/splaytree"]}],"kind":"symbol","seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/RedBlackTree","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap"],"anchor":"Sorted-sets","generated":true,"title":"Sorted sets"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SplayTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A splay tree keeps no balance information. Any sequence of "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" insertions, removals and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accesses on "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" elements costs O(("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}]},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") in all, so each takes O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"amortized, and recently or frequently accessed elements stay near the root: accessing the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements in ascending order costs O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") in all. Reads ("},{"code":"contains(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the bounds, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subscripts and iteration) leave the tree as it is, so they keep the value semantics and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API of the other sorted sets, and take time proportional to the element’s depth, which a run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of ascending insertions can make "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree\/access(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to look an element up and splay it."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var recent: SplayTree = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]","recent.access(40)             \/\/ 40, now at the root","recent.contains(25)           \/\/ false, and the tree is unchanged","let parts = recent.split(at: 30)","Array(parts.lower)            \/\/ [10, 20]","Array(parts.upper)            \/\/ [30, 40, 50]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The elements are a random-access collection in ascending order, indexed by rank like an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tree[0]"},{"type":"text","text":" is the smallest element. The vertices live in flat arrays with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int32"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"links, so the tree holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1 elements, and copying it copies a few arrays only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when one copy is mutated."}]}]}],"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SK","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Sl","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Se","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SE","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s25ExpressibleByArrayLiteralP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SH","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Sk","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/ST","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s10SetAlgebraP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree\/Split"],"anchor":"Structures","generated":true,"title":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree\/init()","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree\/init(_:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree\/height"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree\/access(_:)","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree\/contains(_:)","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree\/elements(in:)-3nita","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree\/elements(in:)-6do42","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/B